examples.question_text:
$AC$ is a diameter of a circle with centre $O$ and radius $6.5$ cm. $B$ lies on the circle and $AB=12$ cm.
(a) Find $BC$.
(b) In a separate circle, $AC$ is a diameter and $\angle BAC=42^{\circ}$. Find $\angle BCA$.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (A) at (-2,0);\coordinate (C) at (2,0);\coordinate (B) at (1.408,1.420);\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\draw (O) circle (2);\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--cycle;\fill (O) circle (0.035);
\node[left] at (A) {$A$};\node[right] at (C) {$C$};\node[above right] at (B) {$B$};\node[below] at (O) {$O$};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]

