$O$ is the centre of a circle. Equal chords $AB$ and $CD$ have perpendicular distances $OE$ and $OF$ from the centre. $OE=6.4$ cm. Find $OF$.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);\coordinate (A) at (-1.2,1.6);\coordinate (B) at (-1.2,-1.6);\coordinate (C) at (1.2,1.6);\coordinate (D) at (1.2,-1.6);\coordinate (E) at (-1.2,0);\coordinate (F) at (1.2,0);
\draw (O) circle (2);\draw (A)--(B);\draw (C)--(D);\draw (E)--(O)--(F);\fill (O) circle (0.035);
\draw (-1.2,0.18)--(-1.02,0.18)--(-1.02,0);\draw (1.2,0.18)--(1.02,0.18)--(1.02,0);
\draw (-1.30,0.8)--(-1.10,0.8);\draw (1.10,0.8)--(1.30,0.8);
\node[above left] at (A) {$A$};\node[below left] at (B) {$B$};\node[above right] at (C) {$C$};\node[below right] at (D) {$D$};\node[left] at (E) {$E$};\node[right] at (F) {$F$};\node[below] at (O) {$O$};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]

$AC$ is a diameter of a circle with centre $O$ and radius $17$ cm. Chord $BD$ is perpendicular to $AC$ at $M$, and $BD=30$ cm.
(a) Find $OM$.
(b) $M$ lies between $A$ and $O$. Find $AM$.
(c) In another circle of radius $17$ cm, a chord is perpendicular to a diameter at a point $5$ cm from the nearer endpoint of the diameter. Find the chord length.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);\coordinate (A) at (-2,0);\coordinate (C) at (2,0);\coordinate (M) at (-0.9412,0);\coordinate (B) at (-0.9412,1.7647);\coordinate (D) at (-0.9412,-1.7647);
\draw (O) circle (2);\draw (A)--(C);\draw (B)--(D);\fill (O) circle (0.035);
\draw (-0.9412,0.18)--(-0.7612,0.18)--(-0.7612,0);
\node[left] at (A) {$A$};\node[right] at (C) {$C$};\node[above] at (B) {$B$};\node[below] at (D) {$D$};\node[below left] at (M) {$M$};\node[below right] at (O) {$O$};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
(a) The perpendicular from the centre bisects the chord, so $BM=30\div2=15\text{ cm}$. Construct radius $OB$.
$\begin{aligned}OM^2&=OB^2-BM^2\\&=17^2-15^2\\&=64\\OM&=8\text{ cm}\end{aligned}$
(b) $AM=OA-OM=17-8=9\text{ cm}$.
(c) The distance from the centre to the chord is $17-5=12\text{ cm}$. The perpendicular bisects the chord.
$\begin{aligned}\text{Half-chord length}&=\sqrt{17^2-12^2}\\&=\sqrt{145}\text{ cm}\\\text{Chord length}&=2\sqrt{145}\text{ cm}\end{aligned}$
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);\coordinate (M) at (-0.9412,0);\coordinate (B) at (-0.9412,1.7647);\coordinate (D) at (-0.9412,-1.7647);
\draw (O) circle (2);\draw (-2,0)--(2,0);\draw (B)--(D);\draw[dashed] (O)--(B);\fill (O) circle (0.035);
\draw (-0.9412,0.18)--(-0.7612,0.18)--(-0.7612,0);
\node[above] at (B) {$B$};\node[below] at (D) {$D$};\node[below left] at (M) {$M$};\node[below right] at (O) {$O$};\node[right] at (-0.40,0.95) {$17\text{ cm}$};\node[left] at (-2.15,0.88) {$15\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]

